// The slate palette. Shadows data/styles/00-theme.otui while the skin is mounted (SKIN
// in init.lua); same roles, same rule -- chrome only, a colour with meaning never lives
// here. The fills follow the tone ladder in tools/skin-generators/make_slate.ps1
// ($Look.Tone) so a Lua-painted panel matches a generated one. Everything is neutral grey
// on the cold side; text is bone rather than parchment and the accent is pewter, so
// nothing in the chrome catches a warm light the way `carved` does.

&textColor: #c6cad0
&textBright: #eef2f6
&textDim: #8a8e95
&textDisabled: #c6cad055
&textMuted: #64686f

&panelFill: #18191b
&panelFillDark: #101113
&panelFillDeep: #090a0b
&panelFillRaised: #212225
&panelFillLight: #2a2b2f

&borderColor: #3a3c41
&borderLight: #5a5d63
&separatorColor: #0e0f11

&selectionFill: #3a4149
&selectionText: #eef2f6
&hoverOverlay: #8a93a022

// The three lines the stock mini-window style paints under a container's header: a 1-px
// highlight, a 1-px shadow and a 1-px border. All off here -- a top bar in this skin is
// one plain plate of stone with the title on it, and the header image draws no line of
// its own either (make_slate.ps1, $Look.HeaderRing).
&headerBevelLight: #00000000
&headerBevelShadow: #00000000
&headerBorderColor: #00000000
